(WEB TECHNOLOGY - STUDY NOTES) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. INTRODUCTION TO WEB TECHNOLOGY) Tj
T*
(Web technology includes tools and languages used to create websites.) Tj
T*
(Examples: HTML, CSS, JavaScript and web servers.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. INTERNET AND WORLD WIDE WEB) Tj
T*
(Internet is a global network of connected computers.) Tj
T*
(WWW is a collection of linked web pages accessed through the Internet.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. HTML) Tj
T*
(HTML stands for HyperText Markup Language.) Tj
T*
(It defines the structure of a web page.) Tj
T*
(Common tags: html, head, title, body, h1, p, a, img and table.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. CSS) Tj
T*
(CSS stands for Cascading Style Sheets.) Tj
T*
(It controls colours, fonts, spacing and webpage layouts.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5. JAVASCRIPT) Tj
T*
(JavaScript makes web pages interactive.) Tj
T*
(It handles button clicks, form validation and dynamic content.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(6. CLIENT-SERVER ARCHITECTURE) Tj
T*
(The browser sends a request to a server.) Tj
T*
(The server processes the request and sends a response.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(7. HTTP AND HTTPS) Tj
T*
(HTTP is used for communication between browsers and servers.) Tj
T*
(HTTPS provides encrypted and secure communication.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(8. STATIC AND DYNAMIC WEBSITES) Tj
T*
(Static websites display mostly fixed content.) Tj
T*
(Dynamic websites can change content based on user input.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(9. WEB HOSTING AND DOMAIN) Tj
T*
(Web hosting stores website files on a server.) Tj
T*
(A domain name is the address used to access a website.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(10. RESPONSIVE WEB DESIGN) Tj
T*
(Responsive design adjusts websites to different screen sizes.) Tj
T*
(It supports mobile phones, tablets and desktop computers.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(REVISION QUESTIONS) Tj
T*
(1. Define web technology.) Tj
T*
(2. What is HTML?) Tj
T*
(3. Explain the uses of CSS.) Tj
T*
(4. What is JavaScript?) Tj
T*
(5. Differentiate HTTP and HTTPS.) Tj
T*
(6. Explain client-server architecture.) Tj
ET
